**Standing lines:** No message to any human. **Jira: 0 reads, 0 writes.** No PR: Tuesday opens it and lands it through CodeQL (never bypass, never dismiss an alert). No `az`, no ssh beyond git over the deploy key, no docker, no deploy, and no HTTP to any hosted, demo, UAT or production host: every measurement is on your local clone; the only network reads are `gh api -X GET`, `git` over the deploy key and the npm registry (`npm ci`, `npm audit`, `npm view`). Never delete (`rm`, `branch -d`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `checkout -- <file>`, `sed -i`): MOVE it to `.tools/b1695/_quarantine/`; no amend, rebase or force-push. **This phase builds no integration with HP tools (Security Manager API, Fleet Threat Assessment, firmware tools, SIEM); next-phase items are stored and architected only. Nothing deploys.** **Git identity is never overridden.** No `cd` (a hook refuses it): absolute single-quoted paths (the folder name !CODING has an exclamation mark), git with `--no-optional-locks` for look-ups, `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count, python with `-I -B`. Every count, file:line pointer and clock in STATUS is produced by a program. A closed list (the owned paths, the allowed commands, the planted shapes) is stated by its PROPERTY first and then "at least these"; any other shape: prove it meets the property or STOP. `always-verify-and-check` and `no-skip-on-failure`: a failure is fixed at the root and re-verified, never skipped.

## CONTEXT BAND AND HANDOVER
At about 70% context, start no new step. At about 75%, stop at a safe boundary: files whole, every process you started stopped by pid, the lock released, `head` clean or its edits named. Write `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/HPSM-POC/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-18_B1695_HANDOVER.md` (done / in hand / next / processes left / decisions a successor keeps: the base sha, the entry text, the Step 3 results so far). Its last line is `HANDOVER B1695: next step <n> | done steps <list>`; end STATUS with the same line.

## HARD STOP (slot)
At the HARD STOP clock of the Stamp: start nothing new, push nothing unproven. A committed but unpushed head is `CODED-UNPROVEN <branch> <sha40>` in STATUS with the steps that ran. Write the HANDOVER and end on its line.

## STATUS and the last line
**Sections:** STATUS-NOW at the top; BLUF; slots as read; PRIOR WORK; BASE AT MAIN (Step 2 counts, the real red); BUILT (the diff); RED-FIRST (Step 3, each run); RUNS AT HEAD (Step 4, each job beside main's, with load1); CHECKS (Step 5); FOR TUESDAY; resources created and removed; the outside-the-fences disclosure.
**LAST line, exactly one of:** `READY B1695: <head sha40>` (equal to `git ls-remote` of the branch) | `HANDOVER B1695: next step <n> | done steps <list>` | `STOPPED: <reason>` | `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`. While running, the last line is `PROGRESS B1695: <step>`.

## STATUS-NOW (the seat keeps this at the top of STATUS)
The step, the lock state (holder text or "mine"), load1, the last command, the next one, and the HARD STOP clock.

## Stamp
Tuesday fills each slot at launch: one word, clock or answer each.
- STAMP: ____
- HEADS AT LAUNCH (origin main full sha, `36c557ad9255125793bfeb99abdea3b0b4d988e2` at drafting; the open PRs, 0 at drafting; whether `b1695*` exists; whether any HPSM lane has landed since): ____
- LAUNCH WINDOW: ____
- HARD STOP (READY target 180 minutes after your Step-0 date; the HARD STOP clock): ____
- Q-ANSWERS (drafter Q-1 to Q-4; defaults: Q-1 date 2026-12-18 is the last allowed day; Q-2 gate G1; Q-3 the zod row takes the empty list; Q-4 the ruling's record is not this lane's): ____
- IDENTITY (the clone-local `user.name` and `user.email` the seat copies, equal to what the project's configured identity prints; else STOP before the first commit): copy by program the project's 2_Project_Files checkout's local user.name and user.email into the clone's local config; print lengths and equality only, never the values; an empty value is a STOP before the first commit.
- GATE-ROUND (G1 as drafted; Q-2): ____

